# `"a\"b"` - the escape ends the body, it does not extend it.
#
# The C stops a body at a backslash whenever the family interpolates, and
# hands the escape itself to the grammar; the two halves `a` and `b` are two
# answers with the escape sequence between them. A reader that treated `\"`
# as one content byte would report one body of five bytes and a close where
# the grammar has an escape, so the count of bodies is what discriminates.
roots 1
mends 0
holds quoted_content
spans quoted_content 5 6
spans quoted_content 8 9
